# Copy to apps/driver/.env (gitignored) for local runs. Expo CLI loads it and
# app.config.js reads it. On EAS these are project secrets, not env entries in
# eas.json — eas.json is committed, so a key there would leak just like app.json
# did.
#
# Both must be MOBILE-restricted keys with only the Maps SDK enabled:
#   Android — Application restriction "Android apps": package
#             com.orderhubsolutions.driver + the release signing SHA-1
#             (`eas credentials` → Android → Keystore shows the SHA-1).
#   iOS     — Application restriction "iOS apps": bundle ID
#             com.orderhubsolutions.driver.
# Never reuse the server key (the one with Geocoding enabled) here.
GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY_ANDROID=
GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY_IOS=
